        "3": "7566b2a815b97bbf101c880838009bbabc4c858b2b054357e33bd3d4a4c86cc0",
        "4": "7566b2a815b97bbf101c880838009bbabc4c858b2b054357e33bd3d4a4c86cc0",
        "5": "7566b2a815b97bbf101c880838009bbabc4c858b2b054357e33bd3d4a4c86cc0"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "ec2-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Suppose your web app needs its own operating system settings. Amazon E C two gives you a virtual server in A W S. You choose its starting software and size, and you control what runs on it.",
          "text_sha256": "f177c3092e40f6e825caedc5c72efd1f069ae3fce052fac53aafc3603be44d6b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b10b1e77868193a6bf22de10620dc4367348a442cba69b364c96a3c53ac9403d",
          "asset_sha256": "7566b2a815b97bbf101c880838009bbabc4c858b2b054357e33bd3d4a4c86cc0"
        },
        {
          "id": "ec2-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Start with an Amazon Machine Image, or A M I. Think of it as a starting template for the operating system, and sometimes other software. Then choose an instance type for the C P U and memory your app needs.",
          "text_sha256": "80e703f56fc1e8b1bb11859ac4f5373316add982e1eb3f96b6e1bcc51e77d5f1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "120b20d282358315fed4e4045153529f5f492574c46de59fc02e7f01c7ff6c0e",
          "asset_sha256": "7566b2a815b97bbf101c880838009bbabc4c858b2b054357e33bd3d4a4c86cc0"
        },
        {
          "id": "ec2-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "An E B S volume can hold your operating system or application data. Its data survives a stop and restart. Termination is different: a volume configured to delete on termination is removed.",
          "text_sha256": "6e13e463529e044a011b53cb265e4e239b2964b847286774125089a5731e23d9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d389772757c4ed15862af81f75be28ee4cf407622535ae2ece2f0eae9e8bac82",
          "asset_sha256": "7566b2a815b97bbf101c880838009bbabc4c858b2b054357e33bd3d4a4c86cc0"
        },
        {
          "id": "ec2-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "A security group is the instance's network firewall. For this web app, allow the traffic it needs, such as H T T P S. You still manage the guest operating system and apply its security patches.",
          "text_sha256": "d87ce94dd1773083a2a667be048f194cb5debe587e54c438125a9bb9c25e3c27",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2a85769824453cd7ccbb9f493191667ca1c7c60c1afc8d9b727e35b02dab3fb1",
          "asset_sha256": "7566b2a815b97bbf101c880838009bbabc4c858b2b054357e33bd3d4a4c86cc0"
        },
        {
          "id": "ec2-05",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "Choose E C two when you want server-level control. If you don't need to manage the operating system, compare a managed service before taking on that work.",
          "text_sha256": "d0db48959ceb87e996cdf213a6898c6429e17d754ae571df55d7b64f91cad6d5",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fb01f4ded000e238033c24bf5e67868a25e4e6fca8375318101d1d401d723558",
          "asset_sha256": "7566b2a815b97bbf101c880838009bbabc4c858b2b054357e33bd3d4a4c86cc0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "92",
      "revision": "m09p92-sap-intro-ec2-route53-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b",
        "2": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b",
        "3": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b",
        "4": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b",
        "5": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "route53-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "How does a browser find the web app behind a name? Amazon Route fifty-three is a managed D N S service. It can register domains, host D N S records, and answer queries about those names.",
          "text_sha256": "d6b101db34ff6dd4925bf51a5aa86468e4c22869e3de9c641a97441295c9c452",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "562d602a7b1517591601f263d07462df78d58a48c3843a004aa7455f96e0d818",
          "asset_sha256": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b"
        },
        {
          "id": "route53-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Say the browser needs app dot example dot com. Its D N S resolver looks up the name. If it has no cached answer, it can ask the authoritative Route fifty-three servers for that hosted zone.",
          "text_sha256": "8e96bed39a4dddc2f82804d4c8b94a379974de4637233041f3e69698cdca6e94",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "553cc217712ed2345bdfb75d83aca9be550d3f669b1cd4d0061be1f8229ea82a",
          "asset_sha256": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b"
        },
        {
          "id": "route53-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The hosted zone's A record points to one ninety-two dot zero dot two dot forty-two. The D N S answer goes back to the browser. Then the browser opens an H T T P S connection to the application endpoint, not to Route fifty-three.",
          "text_sha256": "4886ecc90ef7ff2d0b846f2a7f6a5c40f00df444799066b8ccb13f92673501b3",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5da85952834811e308bad1f7e7f665c88f21f7cc5ea3588329fd8d588df27136",
          "asset_sha256": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b"
        },
        {
          "id": "route53-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Route fifty-three can use health checks with routing policies to change which D N S answer it returns. Clients may still use a cached answer until it expires. D N S failover is not always immediate.",
          "text_sha256": "27763ff4b59c680e26c08fc3bd0f485f6297008bfafe6c37dfed8d5b09ca02e0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "98ff6d5c3489727a6d07eb685d0315005bc7aab1ff996043cab0f3b821ea0f47",
          "asset_sha256": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b"
        },
        {
          "id": "route53-05",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "Remember the boundary: Route fifty-three gives out D N S answers. It does not carry web requests. For D N S across private A W S networks and on premises, look at Route fifty-three Resolver.",
          "text_sha256": "5bd23b4a62df6ecc816f8e34acc3f7ed53917d048f5c9d8af286acddcecde8a2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d2e95033f011e9705f77fd412b5464c12a345ed71f350a8875c8c16c35c686ee",
          "asset_sha256": "5e52de68314b46c9eb3bd21dd7651a39432684ad1dcf2a6d4db9062e05f54b5b"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
